# Copy to deploy/mail/cloudflare.ini, then: chmod 600 deploy/mail/cloudflare.ini
#
# Easier and safer than editing this file by hand:
#     sudo bash deploy/mail/setup-mail.sh --set-token
# which reads the token from a hidden prompt, validates its character set,
# and writes the file with the right mode. The Hetzner web console rewrites
# some characters on paste, which corrupts a token silently — the file then
# looks plausible and Cloudflare rejects it with error 1000.
#
# Create the token at Cloudflare → My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token
#   Template:       "Edit zone DNS"
#   Permissions:    Zone / DNS / Edit   AND   Zone / Zone / Read
#   Zone Resources: Include / Specific zone / robustuavs.ai
#
# Both permissions are required. certbot looks the zone up by name before it
# writes the challenge record, so a DNS:Edit-only token fails at the first
# API call with an error that does not mention permissions.
#
# Used only by certbot for the DNS-01 challenge: it writes a temporary
# _acme-challenge TXT record and removes it again. It is not used to publish
# any of the permanent mail records — those you add by hand from the table
# setup-mail.sh prints, so nothing automated can rewrite your zone.
dns_cloudflare_api_token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE
